{
  "decision": "NO_CHANGE",
  "workflow_yaml": null,
  "rationale": "No supported optimization safely applies to this workflow. The workflow already caches dependency downloads via setup-node (cache: yarn) and reuses a validated scratch-organ environment through actions/cache/restore/save, so P-LIT-GHA-CACHE and P-LIT-ENV-CACHE are already reflected. P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT does not help: nuts-org already has timeout-minutes: 150, successful runs complete in about 7-8 minutes per history, and the long cap is a deliberate safety net because Salesforce deployments can take ~20 minutes and mocha allows 30 minutes per test; lowering it risks false timeouts on valid slow runs (contraindication: valid slow runs exceed the limit) and would not reduce normal run time. P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE is contraindicated: concurrency.cancel-in-progress is intentionally false to avoid competing for the scratch-org quota and deployment lock, matching the workflow's stated design. P-LIT-FAIL-SCHEDULE is not triggered because the recent scheduled runs all succeeded (no repeated-failure streak). P-LIT-CHANGE-FILTER and P-LIT-SKIP-WORKFLOW are behavior-changing and required checks are not verified, so omitting runs could drop needed org validation. The Bazel patterns do not apply because this is a Node/Salesforce workflow with no Bazel build.",
  "evidence_ids": ["P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT", "P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE", "P-LIT-GHA-CACHE", "P-LIT-ENV-CACHE", "P-LIT-FAIL-SCHEDULE", "P-LIT-CHANGE-FILTER"]
}
